Dataset raw name: Two-Decades Brainclinics Archive for Insights in Neurophysiology (TD-BRAIN)
Dataset Link: https://brainclinics.com/resources  (3.1 version)
Paper Link: https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-022-01409-z

Short name: TDBrain-ODD (only use oddball task)





III. Output Format

Each subject/session's processed data is saved as:

- `X.dat`: EEG data with shape `(N, T, C)`
- `y.dat`: Corresponding labels with shape `(N, 4)`
- `meta.json`: Metadata containing channel names, sampling rate, task information, and other relevant information

Where:
- `N`: number of trials
- `T`: number of time points per trial, e.g., 250 for a 1-second epoch at 250 Hz
- `C`: number of EEG channels

Label Structure (`y`):

Each label row contains:

`[disease_id, stimulus_type, subject_id, task_id]`

Where:
- `disease_id`: `-1`, set to unknown for now, wait for full ERP dataset release
- `stimulus_type`: 0: "standard", 1: "target"
- `subject_id`: numeric identifier derived from `sub-XXX`
- `task_id`: 1 visual oddball

